# UI Components Skill

## Purpose
Enforce consistency in the `@tbe/components` shared component library. All reusable UI elements live here. This skill ensures props are typed via `@tbe/interface`, animations use Framer Motion, variants are string unions not booleans, and loading states are handled uniformly.

## Rules
1. **Always import prop types from `@tbe/interface`** — define the interface there first, then import it.
2. **Never use inline `style={{}}` props** for static styling — use Tailwind classes only. Framer Motion `animate`/`initial`/`exit` props are the only exception.
3. **Always use the `Button` component** from `packages/components/src/common/Buttons/Button.tsx` for interactive buttons — never create ad-hoc `<button>` elements in new components.
4. **Variants must be string union literals** — not booleans. Use `variant: "PRIMARY" | "SECONDARY" | "OUTLINE" | "GHOST" | "SUCCESS" | "NEUTRAL"`.
5. **Always handle `isLoading` state** — show `<LoadingSpinner />` from `packages/components/src/common/LoadingSpinner` when loading.
6. **Export all new components from `packages/components/src/index.ts`** — no deep imports allowed by consumers.
7. **Page-level layout components must use `<PageLayout>`** — never wrap pages in raw `<main>` or `<div>` in consuming apps.
8. **Animation must use `framer-motion`** — no CSS `@keyframes` in component files.
9. **Component files must be PascalCase** — `MyComponent.tsx`, not `my-component.tsx`.
10. **JSDoc the props interface** with a one-line description per prop — no wall-of-text.

## Patterns

### Standard shared component structure
```tsx
// packages/components/src/common/MyWidget/MyWidget.tsx
import type { MyWidgetProps } from "@tbe/interface"; // 1. Props from @tbe/interface
import { motion } from "framer-motion";
import LoadingSpinner from "../LoadingSpinner";

const MyWidget = ({
  title,
  isLoading = false,
  variant = "PRIMARY",
  onClick,
}: MyWidgetProps) => {
  if (isLoading) return <LoadingSpinner />;

  return (
    <motion.div
      initial={{ opacity: 0 }}
      animate={{ opacity: 1 }}
      className="rounded-lg p-4 bg-white"
    >
      <h3 className="text-heading font-semibold">{title}</h3>
    </motion.div>
  );
};

export default MyWidget;
```

### Defining the props interface in @tbe/interface
```ts
// packages/interface/src/Components.ts
export interface MyWidgetProps {
  /** Title text displayed in the widget header */
  title: string;
  /** Shows loading spinner instead of content */
  isLoading?: boolean;
  /** Visual style variant */
  variant?: "PRIMARY" | "SECONDARY" | "OUTLINE";
  /** Click handler */
  onClick?: () => void;
}
```

### Button usage
```tsx
// CORRECT
import Button from "@tbe/components/common/Buttons/Button";

<Button
  variant="PRIMARY"
  text="Submit"
  active={!isSubmitting}
  isLoading={isSubmitting}
  onClick={handleSubmit}
/>

// Also correct for navigation
import LinkButton from "@tbe/components/common/Buttons/LinkButton";
<LinkButton href="/dashboard" buttonProps={{ variant: "OUTLINE", text: "Dashboard" }} />
```

## Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Raw button element with inline styles
```tsx
// BAD — never do this
<button
  style={{ backgroundColor: "#4f46e5", color: "white", padding: "8px 16px" }}
  onClick={handleClick}
>
  Click me
</button>
```
```tsx
// GOOD
import Button from "@tbe/components/common/Buttons/Button";
<Button variant="PRIMARY" text="Click me" active onClick={handleClick} />
```

### ❌ Boolean variant prop
```tsx
// BAD
interface BadButtonProps { isPrimary?: boolean; isOutline?: boolean; }
```
```tsx
// GOOD
interface GoodButtonProps { variant: "PRIMARY" | "OUTLINE" | "GHOST"; }
```

### ❌ Deep import bypassing index.ts
```tsx
// BAD — never import this way from consuming apps
import Button from "@tbe/components/src/common/Buttons/Button";
```
```tsx
// GOOD
import { Button } from "@tbe/components";
```
